# 7. SMART AUTOFILL ENGINE

This is the most important technical component.

Build a reusable, modular autofill engine.

## 7.1 Website Detection

Detect:
- Hostname.
- Supported domain.
- Application path.
- Current form type.
- Available form fields.
- Extension permission status.

Never run on unsupported websites.

Never assume a website is supported solely because its page title matches.

## 7.2 Form Scanner

Inspect:
- Input elements.
- Textareas.
- Select elements.
- Radio groups.
- Checkboxes.
- Associated labels.
- Name attributes.
- ID attributes.
- Placeholder attributes.
- Accessible labels.
- Visible field descriptions.

Support Bengali and English labels.

## 7.3 Field Mapping

Implement a mapping engine using:

1. Exact field name.
2. Exact field ID.
3. Associated label.
4. Normalized label matching.
5. Bengali synonym matching.
6. Placeholder matching.
7. Context-aware matching.

Each mapping must have:
- Source property.
- Target element.
- Confidence level.
- Matching explanation.
- Verification status.

Confidence levels:
- High.
- Medium.
- Low.
- Unmatched.

High-confidence mappings can be proposed for autofill.

Medium-confidence mappings require user confirmation.

Low-confidence mappings must never be automatically filled.

## 7.4 Autofill Execution

Workflow:

1. Detect supported website.
2. Verify supported application path.
3. Scan the form.
4. Generate field mappings.
5. Load selected profile.
6. Match profile properties.
7. Check field compatibility.
8. Show preview.
9. Require user approval.
10. Fill approved fields.
11. Dispatch appropriate input and change events.
12. Verify resulting field values.
13. Generate a completion report.

Support:
- Text.
- Email.
- Telephone.
- Date.
- Textarea.
- Select.
- Radio.
- Checkbox.

Handle dynamic forms using MutationObserver where necessary.

Support controlled framework inputs only when their behavior has been tested.

Never directly manipulate framework internals or bypass website validation.

## 7.5 Dropdown Matching

Implement safe option matching.

Compare:
- Visible option text.
- Option value.
- Normalized spelling.
- Bengali and English equivalents.

Do not select an option when multiple candidates are ambiguous.

Show unresolved dropdowns to the user.

Never invent a dropdown value.

## 7.6 Date Conversion

Support:
- MM/DD/YYYY.
- DD/MM/YYYY.
- YYYY-MM-DD.

Detect expected target format before conversion.

Prevent invalid date transformations.

Preserve the user's original date.

